title: "The parity conjecture for independence polynomials of generalized Petersen graphs contradicts itself"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bhattacharjee
    given-names: Deep
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0466-750X"
    affiliation: "Formerly, Electro-Gravitational Space Propulsion Laboratory (EGSPL), Bhubaneswar, Odisha 751030, India"
    email: d.bhattacharjee@erl-forschung.de
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-09
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/creelie/eConjectureGPParity"
keywords:
  - independence polynomial
  - real roots
  - generalized Petersen graph
  - graph isomorphism
  - counterexample
abstract: >-
  It has been conjectured that for n >= 2k+1 the independence polynomial of
  the generalized Petersen graph GP(n,k) has only real roots if and only if k
  is even. Erlbacher's Demonstrandum project refuted it first, with GP(7,3),
  GP(9,2) and GP(7,2) = GP(7,3). We show that the statement contradicts itself: GP(n,2) is
  isomorphic to GP(n,(n-1)/2) whenever n = 3 (mod 4), and (n-1)/2 is then
  odd, and give hand proofs that each direction fails on its own, at GP(7,3)
  and at GP(9,2).
